  "semantic_justification": {
    "defect_identity": "Issue #148 and PR #158 concern @DependencyEndpoint generating invalid Swift for fatalError-based defaults. The retained fix handles the same missing-return expansion defect for the Void plus immediately-invoked-closure subcase exercised by the fixing commit's test.",
    "pre_pr_baseline_evidence": {
      "repository_bundle": "sources/repository.bundle",
      "repository_bundle_sha256": "4a30b22f9976c50b3a72fa0065bc0b3049e2e33b9bc945c43eec21dfd73c2527",
      "pr_base_commit": "6c2bbde0b2bfaa2f9dc800ecc9c9af00337029cc",
      "pr_base_tree": "4dbd7105841f74fbd03016a4dba31e98cfb04450",
      "source_path": "Sources/DependenciesMacrosPlugin/DependencyEndpointMacro.swift",
      "source_blob": "742b3efc92884693d714ba768af816292e5d2ab9",
      "ancestry_check": "git merge-base 6c2bbde 9b56680 equals 6c2bbde0b2bfaa2f9dc800ecc9c9af00337029cc",
      "pre_existing_condition": "At lines 79-83 of the PR-base source, the rewrite is guarded by `if !functionType.isVoid, closure.statements.count == 1, ...`; therefore the Void path exclusion predates the PR branch and was not introduced by the selected intra-PR buggy revision."
    },
    "trigger_relation": "The declared trigger changes the existing upstream fatalError macro-expansion case to `() -> Void = { { fatalError() }() }`. On the buggy revision the pre-existing Void guard suppresses the return rewrite; the retained production hunk permits that rewrite when the expression is an immediately-invoked closure. This uses only the pre-existing @DependencyEndpoint API.",
    "scope_note": "The unrelated `}fixes:` whitespace correction is test-only, outside the sole declared trigger selector, and absent from the minimized production patch."
  },
